WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:05.821
Miles pulled Edward away from City Hall.

2
00:00:05.822 --> 00:00:11.505
Heading toward the river, they heard the same news being passed from one person to another.

3
00:00:11.506 --> 00:00:16.343
"Have you heard? The king is dead!"

4
00:00:16.344 --> 00:00:20.827
The words made Edward shudder, and tears came to his eyes.

5
00:00:20.828 --> 00:00:27.402
The man who had been such a tyrant to others had always been gentle with him.

6
00:00:27.403 --> 00:00:32.622
"The country has lost a king, but I have lost a father."

7
00:00:32.623 --> 00:00:36.039
Edward wiped away a tear with his hand.

8
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:42.122
Miles patted Edward on the back while encouraging him to hurry.

9
00:00:42.123 --> 00:00:47.226
"Long live the king!" a man shouted as they stepped onto the bridge.

10
00:00:47.227 --> 00:00:52.280
"Long live King Edward!" others shouted.

11
00:00:52.281 --> 00:00:55.111
"That's me!" Edward said.

12
00:00:55.112 --> 00:01:00.872
"How strange and wonderful it seems at the same time!"

13
00:01:00.873 --> 00:01:06.959
Miles frowned. "Something is wrong with this boy," he thought.

14
00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.346
"He believes he's the king."

15
00:01:11.347 --> 00:01:15.601
Miles decided to go along with the pauper's fantasy for now.

16
00:01:15.602 --> 00:01:19.594
"Yes, Your Highness."

17
00:01:19.595 --> 00:01:24.800
Edward stopped walking and waited for Miles to stop and turn around.

18
00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:33.183
"Actually, now that I'm king," Edward said, "you should address me as 'Your Majesty' or 'sir.'

19
00:01:33.184 --> 00:01:37.659
By the way, where are we going?"

20
00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:41.999
Miles walked back to where Edward was standing.

21
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.851
"To an inn on the other side of the bridge.

22
00:01:44.852 --> 00:01:51.138
Then after a meal and a good night's sleep, we'll head to Hendon Hall, my family's home in the country.

23
00:01:51.139 --> 00:01:54.908
You'll be safe there, Your Majesty."

24
00:01:54.909 --> 00:01:57.118
"I'd prefer to go to the palace and—"

25
00:01:57.119 --> 00:02:04.149
"So," a voice growled suddenly, "you finally decided to show up!"

26
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:07.994
John Canty reached out a hand to seize Edward.

27
00:02:07.995 --> 00:02:12.129
"You won't escape again! If you do, I'll—"

28
00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:17.334
Miles stepped between them. "Not so fast, my friend.

29
00:02:17.335 --> 00:02:21.321
You don't need to be so hard on the boy.

30
00:02:21.322 --> 00:02:24.556
And why are you bothering him anyway?"

31
00:02:24.557 --> 00:02:28.409
"Not that it's any of your business, but he's my son."

32
00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:33.745
"You're lying!" Edward peered around Miles to glare at John.

33
00:02:33.746 --> 00:02:39.478
"I hate you, and I'd rather die than go anywhere with you!"

34
00:02:39.479 --> 00:02:45.292
"Then it's settled," Miles said. "The boy stays with me."

35
00:02:45.293 --> 00:02:50.592
"We'll see about that!" John tried to push past Miles to reach Edward.

36
00:02:50.593 --> 00:02:56.008
But Miles raised one arm to block John and put his other hand on his sword.

37
00:02:56.009 --> 00:03:00.828
"Don't even think of touching this lad!" Miles warned.

38
00:03:00.829 --> 00:03:04.673
"I just saved him from being thrown in the river.

39
00:03:04.674 --> 00:03:09.064
I'm not going to let you do something worse to him!"

40
00:03:09.065 --> 00:03:14.105
For a moment John looked like he might challenge Miles.

41
00:03:14.106 --> 00:03:19.680
But then, muttering curses and threats, he moved away.

42
00:03:19.681 --> 00:03:24.103
"Phew! That was close!" Edward said.

43
00:03:24.104 --> 00:03:28.764
"That man keeps mistaking me for his son."

44
00:03:28.765 --> 00:03:33.820
"Don't worry, Your Majesty," Miles said as they crossed the bridge.

45
00:03:33.821 --> 00:03:38.828
"I vow to protect you from all danger and nurse you back to health.

46
00:03:38.829 --> 00:03:42.063
Think of me as your older brother."

47
00:03:42.064 --> 00:03:46.882
"Thank you for your protection, but I'm not sick," Edward said.

48
00:03:46.883 --> 00:03:53.093
"And if you were my older brother, you'd be king instead of me."

49
00:03:53.094 --> 00:03:58.535
"I guess that's right," Miles said slowly.

50
00:03:58.536 --> 00:04:02.956
"Well, here we are at the inn where I'm staying."

51
00:04:02.957 --> 00:04:08.927
Miles ordered some hot food to be sent to his room on the top floor.

52
00:04:08.928 --> 00:04:12.325
Their meal soon arrived.

53
00:04:12.326 --> 00:04:18.687
"We'll have a regular feast." Miles rubbed his hands together in anticipation.

54
00:04:18.688 --> 00:04:22.155
"It may not be as fine as the mayor's banquet, but—"

55
00:04:22.156 --> 00:04:27.372
He was stopped by the sight of Edward standing at the wash basin.

56
00:04:27.373 --> 00:04:30.528
"What are you waiting for, lad?"

57
00:04:30.529 --> 00:04:34.881
"I want to wash my hands and face."

58
00:04:34.882 --> 00:04:41.182
"Oh, is that all? You don't need my permission to do that."

59
00:04:41.183 --> 00:04:46.904
Edward remained motionless, except for impatiently tapping his foot.

60
00:04:46.905 --> 00:04:50.496
"What's the problem?" Miles said.

61
00:04:50.497 --> 00:04:53.621
"The water and the towel are right there."

62
00:04:53.622 --> 00:04:59.996
"Please stop talking and pour the water into the basin," Edward said.

63
00:04:59.997 --> 00:05:06.032
Trying not to laugh, Miles picked up the pitcher and did as he was told.

64
00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:09.406
"My goodness," Miles thought.

65
00:05:09.407 --> 00:05:16.129
"He's acting like he really is a member of the royal family."

66
00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:20.153
"Ahem! I need to dry myself."

67
00:05:20.154 --> 00:05:26.704
Edward raised an eyebrow, indicating the towel that was right in front of him.

68
00:05:26.705 --> 00:05:31.993
Miles obediently handed him the towel.

69
00:05:31.994 --> 00:05:37.568
While Miles washed his own face and hands, Edward sat at the table.

70
00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:41.991
Miles pulled out the other chair and prepared to join him.

71
00:05:41.992 --> 00:05:45.520
"What are you doing?" Edward cried.

72
00:05:45.521 --> 00:05:52.952
"I'm sitting! And no one else sits while the king is sitting—not without the king's permission.

73
00:05:52.953 --> 00:05:57.468
Your role is to serve me."

74
00:05:57.469 --> 00:06:01.366
"Yes, Your Highness. Forgive me."

75
00:06:01.367 --> 00:06:07.118
Amused, Miles stood obediently behind Edward's chair.

76
00:06:07.119 --> 00:06:11.288
As Edward ate, he relaxed and became more friendly.

77
00:06:11.289 --> 00:06:18.344
"I think you said that your name is Miles Hendon?" Edward put down his fork.

78
00:06:18.345 --> 00:06:25.901
"I'd like to know more about you. Please tell me your story."

